    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1357">

                <pb facs="0907" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/159.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Hostetter to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Hermosillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Carranza wires regarding the Associated Press reports regarding action of
                    Villa when he gets to Torreon in treatment of <pb facs="0908" n="792"
                        xml:id="pg792"/> Spaniards: Carranza says Associated Press is not always to
                    be believed, and he does not believe Villa made said statements, as he has
                    notified chief that all foreigners and their properties will be respected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hostetter</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
